[COMMENTS]
STATION,Velocity-area station opened in 1962 and rebuilt after 1968 flood, weir built in 1971. GENERAL: Velocity area station with cableway. Station opened in 10/1962. Hut rebuilt after July 1968 flood. 14m wide informal shallow Flat V weir installed 1971. Initially for Water Resources, more recently considered full range with FCRM interest. STATION HYDROMETRY: Natural control up until weir installed in 1971. Now considered a full range station. Low embankments at field level extend containment. Gabions stabilise bed and banks. Bypassing occurs during exceptional events (>2.1m). Multiple ratings applied across period of record; high flow events in Nov/Dec 2000 altered channel geometry u/s and d/s of station. Ratings after this period include estimates for out of bank flow. FLOW RECORD: Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2020 (WINFAP Files v9). FLOW REGIME: Substantial groundwater and surface water abstractions in catchment for public water supply and industrial/agricultural purposes. Flows increased by effluent returns.
CATCHMENT,Rises in Greensand and Gault Clay of the Blackdown Hills. Predominantly Keuper sandstones and marls. Extensive alluvium and valley gravels lower down. Some heathland, woodland and pasture, and a wide range of agriculture. No major catchment changes.
Qmed Suitability,Good fit to gaugings.
Pooling Suitability,Gauged close to AMAX3. Pre-2000 ratings do not take out of bank flow into account and therefore flows are underestimated.
[END]
